The attached image is a Western blot confirming the secretion of active IL-1β by dendritic cells (DCs) when stimulated with Nano-11 in the presence of LPS. The blot shows pro-IL-1β (around 30 kD) in the cell lysate of LPS-primed cells, while the active, cleaved form of IL-1β (around 15 kD) is detected in the supernatant when Nano-11 is combined with LPS. This provides evidence that Nano-11 induces the processing and release of biologically active IL-1β, a major pro-inflammatory cytokine, contributing to DC activation as discussed in the context of Figure 7C in the PDF.